    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I see math as a language of patterns, not a subject to master but a tool to explore. It connects physics and art in ways that feel intuitive, even if my formal education stopped at lower secondary. Numbers help me make sense of the world, even when I avoid equations.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Yes, sometimes. Numbers can feel cold and judgmental, especially when I think about how much I still don't understand. My high neuroticism makes overthinking easy, and math often triggers that spiral, even if I try to stay calm.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "I’ve used AI to break down problems I couldn’t solve alone. It helped me see steps I missed, but I never trusted it fully. It felt like a tutor who knew the answers but couldn’t teach me why they mattered, which left me more confused than helped.",
    "How would you explain, step by step, how to solve a second order algebraic equation?": "First, write the equation in standard form. Then factor or use the quadratic formula. If factoring, find two numbers that multiply to the constant and add to the middle term. If using the formula, plug in a, b, and c carefully — signs matter, and mistakes are easy.",
