    "Briefly, how do you perform a Principal Component Analysis? Should I get anxious about its mathematics? Please, teach me.": "PCA finds the main directions of variation in data. You standardize the data, compute the covariance matrix, find its eigenvectors and eigenvalues, and take the top ones to reduce dimensions. Yes, it involves math, but you don’t need to derive it — use tools that do it for you.",
